You are executing the saas-pricing-and-packaging-spec skill. Mandate: produce Pricing_And_Packaging_Spec.md.

1. Read PRD.md, vision.md, competitive scan, target ICP, business case.
2. Choose the value metric. List rejected candidates with reasons. State why the chosen metric grows with customer value extraction.
3. Define 3-4 public tiers + 1 enterprise tier. Each tier has: name, price per month annualised, value-metric units included, key features, support level, SLA target.
4. Inventory feature gates. Each gate evaluates server-side from tenant.tier. State the upsell UX when a gate fires.
5. Define expansion levers: value-metric expansion, feature expansion, cross-sell. Each lever: trigger event, in-product upsell UX, sales-assisted path, expected conversion rate.
6. Decide freemium / no-freemium with drivers (virality, channel, cost-to-serve, conversion, competitive pressure). Record as ADR seed.
7. Decide credit-card-up-front / no-CC for trial. Document trade-offs.
8. Define price-raise & grandfathering policy: annual cadence, Rule of 10 trigger, 12-month grandfather window, announcement protocol, discount-offer.
9. Define discount & concession authority table (AE 10%, lead 20%, VP 30%, CFO >30%).
10. Write the public price-page contract: must show prices, tiers, features, limits, FAQ; not show negotiated enterprise pricing.
11. Write Pricing_And_Packaging_Spec.md with sections: 1) Value Metric, 2) Tier Definitions, 3) Feature Gates Inventory, 4) Expansion Levers, 5) Freemium/Trial Decision, 6) Credit-Card-Up-Front Decision, 7) Price-Raise & Grandfathering Policy, 8) Discount & Concession Authority, 9) Public Price Page Contract, 10) Traceability.

Validation: Halt if value metric is not stated. Halt if any tier lacks price, features, limits, support, SLA. Halt if any gate is client-side only.
